{{short description|none}}

This gallery of '''flags of the autonomous communities of Spain''' shows the distinctive [[flag]]s of the 17 [[autonomous communities]] (constitutionally they are the [[nationalities and regions of Spain|nationalities and regions]] in which [[Spain]] is territorially organized), plus the autonomous cities of [[Ceuta]] and [[Melilla]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Ortín García |first=Carmen |date=2025-06-16 |title=«Malum carmen incantare» |url=https://doi.org/10.55104/frdc_0938 |journal=Fundamentos romanísticos del Derecho contemporáneo |issue=10 |doi=10.55104/frdc_0938|doi-access=free }}</ref>

==Flags of the Autonomous Communities ==
<gallery>
File:Flag of Andalucía.svg|Arbonaida, the [[Flag of Andalucia]], depicting a coat of arms on a background with three horizontal stripes (from top: green, white, green).
File:Flag of Aragon.svg|[[Flag of Aragon]], depicting a coat of arms on a background consisting of nine horizontal stripes, alternating yellow and red (with yellow on the top).
File:Flag of Asturias.svg|[[Flag of Asturias|Flag of the]] [[Principality of Asturias]], depicting a yellow cross on a blue background.
File:Flag of the Balearic Islands.svg|[[Flag of Balearic Islands|Flag of]] the [[Balearic Islands]], with a white castle on a rectangular purple background in the top left, with the rest of the flag consisting of nine horizontal stripes, alternating yellow and red, with yellow on the top.
File:Flag of the Basque Country.svg|[[Ikurriña]], the flag of the [[Basque Country (autonomous community)|Basque Country]], consisting of a red background with two perpendicular white lines in the front, as well as two intersecting diagonal green lines.
File:Flag of the Canary Islands.svg|[[Flag of the Canary Islands|Flag of]] the [[Canary Islands]], depicting a coat of arms with two lions on a background consisting of three vertical stripes (from left: white, blue, yellow).
File:Flag of Cantabria.svg|[[Flag of Cantabria]], depicting of a coat of arms on top of a background consisting of two horizontal stripes: white on top and red on the bottom.
File:Flag of Castile-La Mancha.svg|[[Flag of Castilla–La Mancha|Flag of]] [[Castile-La Mancha]], depicting a yellow and blue castle on the right hand side of the flag, above a background consisting of two vertical stripes (from left: red, yellow).
File:Bandera de Castilla y León (heráldica).svg|[[Flag of Castile-Leon|Flag of]] [[Castile and León]], depicting four rectangles in a two-by-two format, the upper left and bottom right of which being red, and the others being white.
File:Flag of Catalonia.svg|The [[Senyera]], the Flag of [[Catalonia]], depicting nine horizontal stripes, alternating yellow and red, beginning with yellow from the top.
File:Flag of Extremadura with COA.svg|[[Flag of Extremadura]], depicting a coat of arms above a background consisting of three horizontal stripes (from top: green, white, black).
File:Flag of Galicia.svg|[[Flag of Galicia]], depicting  a coat of arms above a white background, with a blue stripe going from the top left to the bottom right.
File:Flag of La Rioja (with coat of arms).svg|[[Flag of La Rioja]], depicting a coat of arms above a background consisting of four horizontal stripes (from top: red, white, green, yellow).
File:Flag of the Community of Madrid.svg|[[Flag of the Community of Madrid|Flag of]] [[Madrid (autonomous community)|Madrid]], depicting seven white five-sided stars in two rows (four above and three below), above a red background.
File:Flag of the Region of Murcia.svg|[[Flag of the Region of Murcia|Flag of]] [[Region of Murcia|Murcia]], consisting of a burgundy background with four yellow towers in the top left and seven crowns in the bottom right.
File:Bandera de Navarra.svg|[[Flag of Navarre]], depicting a coat of arms above a red background.
File:Flag of the Valencian Community (2x3).svg|The ''Senyera coronada'', [[Flag of Valencia]], depicting a large blue vertical stripe on the left hand side with yellow decorations, followed by a small red stripe with white and green decorations, followed by nine horizontal stripes, alternating yellow and red, beginning with yellow on the top.
</gallery>
